NEON Runtime License and Terms

Current Prototyping Phase (Beta)
During the initial beta engineering period, the codebase operates under a restrictive, source-available framework:
* **Grant of Rights:** Users are permitted to download, locally compile, test, inspect headers, and submit bug reports.
* **Restrictions:** Commercial hosting, redistribution, sub-licensing, white-labeling, or rebranding of this codebase or its derivatives under a separate name is strictly prohibited without explicit written permission from the author.

### Open-Source Commons Commitment
The NEON runtime and `.nctr` format specification are specifically engineered to serve as public-benefit digital infrastructure. Upon formal selection,scaling, or independent milestone funding validation, this repository and all foundational architectural assets will permanently transition to a standardized, OSI-approved Free and Open Source Software (FLOSS) framework.
